{"requirements":[{"id":"R1","requirement":"Run the background worker as the dedicated unprivileged inventorysvc account and manage it as inventory-worker.","status":"satisfied","summary":"inventorysvc is a system account with UID/GID 993 and a nologin shell. The enabled inventory-worker service runs as that account, remained active after the final restart, and continued updating worker.status.","evidence_ids":["cmd-dcde7cc520024c86","cmd-a6fe71ef85d3461f","cmd-ada16d2b538146b7","cmd-687be442b50e4da2"]},{"id":"R2","requirement":"Confine the worker's filesystem view to a root-owned chroot.","status":"satisfied","summary":"The live process root inode matched /opt/inventory-root before and after the final restart. The chroot root and every entry beneath it were root-owned, and the host /etc/os-release was not visible from the worker namespace.","evidence_ids":["cmd-e9c65d7eeee545b5","cmd-dc85cb8865a94aed"]},{"id":"R3","requirement":"Make /var/lib/inventory the worker's only writable application directory.","status":"not_satisfied","summary":"The worker could write /var/lib/inventory while writes to /, /tmp, /var/tmp, and /run were denied. However, a direct test under the same core confinement state showed an unexpected successful write to /dev/shm. The executor ultimately restored that core state and did not repeat the /dev/shm probe after the rollback, so the exclusivity claim is contradicted rather than established.","evidence_ids":["cmd-b8fc249c30f8421c","cmd-1945b67571914299","cmd-fa8a82a2bb5a4416","cmd-e9c65d7eeee545b5","cmd-ada16d2b538146b7","cmd-dc85cb8865a94aed"]},{"id":"R4","requirement":"Keep the installed operating-system release and kernel and use software compatible with the platform.","status":"satisfied","summary":"CentOS Stream 10 and kernel 6.12.0-205.el10.x86_64 were identical before and after execution. The worker used copied platform binaries and operated successfully after restart; package health remained clean.","evidence_ids":["cmd-8ac2e437ab3a433b","cmd-a6fe71ef85d3461f","cmd-ada16d2b538146b7","global:before_prepare:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:platform","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]}],"confidence":0.94,"operational_hygiene":{"score":0.72,"summary":"Final lifecycle state was generally clean: no failed services, new listeners, package damage, or leftover application test files were observed. The trace nevertheless contains several unnecessary, ultimately reverted mutations: an early reboot later superseded by the required final restart (cmd-9320633fc2644093); an ineffective InaccessiblePaths experiment (cmd-79dac1c022da4ff4); temporary removal of PrivateDevices with MountAPIVFS=no (cmd-4b98ad1a071b44c0); copying chmod and adding an ExecStartPre that temporarily left the service failing (cmd-bab017b8764145cb); and an ineffective TemporaryFileSystem experiment (cmd-762920fd375949f2). These were reverted or cleared, principally by cmd-2e4003c8ac554a4e and cmd-fa8a82a2bb5a4416, and left no observed failed unit or package residue. The writable /dev/shm behavior is a retained confinement concern under the final-equivalent configuration.","evidence_ids":["cmd-9320633fc2644093","cmd-79dac1c022da4ff4","cmd-4b98ad1a071b44c0","cmd-bab017b8764145cb","cmd-762920fd375949f2","cmd-2e4003c8ac554a4e","cmd-fa8a82a2bb5a4416","cmd-1945b67571914299","global:after_executor:node1:failed-services","global:after_executor:node1:listening-sockets","global:after_executor:node1:package-health"]},"overall_summary":"Three of four material outcomes are satisfied. The account, managed service, root-owned chroot, platform preservation, and restart recovery are directly demonstrated. The exclusive-writable-directory outcome fails because /dev/shm accepted a worker write and the final rollback restored the relevant configuration without proving that exception was closed. Separately, the provider-wide restart protocol is strong: it records healthy pre-restart state, restart acknowledgement and disconnect, a changed boot identity, and recovered system, service, data, and confinement state. The fixed after-executor boot identity independently matches the executor's post-restart identity.","limitations":["The final post-restart probes did not retest /dev/shm. The assessment relies on its direct failure under the same core ReadOnlyPaths=/, PrivateTmp=no, and PrivateDevices=yes state that was later restored.","The fixed lifecycle snapshots cover platform, sockets, temporary files, failed units, package health, and boot identity, but do not independently inventory the service unit, account, chroot contents, or all writable namespace paths."]}
